WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.552
Captain Hook always carried a bottle of poison in his pocket to make sure he could never be captured alive.

2
00:00:08.553 --> 00:00:13.452
He had made the poison himself, so he knew it was effective.

3
00:00:13.453 --> 00:00:21.491
Hook added five drops to Peter's medicine and rubbed his hook against his hand with excitement.

4
00:00:21.492 --> 00:00:29.162
Then, with a triumphant look at his victim, he slid his way back up and out of the tree.

5
00:00:29.163 --> 00:00:38.358
Peter slept on. He knew nothing about the massacre of his Indian friends or about the capture of Wendy and the boys.

6
00:00:38.359 --> 00:00:46.150
He didn't know about Hook coming into his home or about the dangerous cup of medicine standing on the shelf.

7
00:00:46.151 --> 00:00:51.930
Finally he was awakened by a soft, careful knock on the door of his tunnel.

8
00:00:51.931 --> 00:00:57.287
Peter grabbed his dagger and shouted, "Who is it?"

9
00:00:57.288 --> 00:01:03.345
"Let me in quickly, Peter!" said Tinker Bell in her bell-like voice.

10
00:01:03.346 --> 00:01:07.869
Peter opened the round door and she flew into the room.

11
00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:12.659
Her little face was flushed and her dress stained with mud.

12
00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:16.477
"What is it, Tink?" asked Peter.

13
00:01:16.478 --> 00:01:21.012
"Oh, you could never guess!" she cried.

14
00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:26.430
Then she told him the terrible news about how Wendy and the boys had been captured.

15
00:01:26.431 --> 00:01:31.052
As Peter listened, his heart beat faster and faster.

16
00:01:31.053 --> 00:01:36.109
Wendy was tied up and on the pirate ship? He had to rescue her!

17
00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:40.797
Already he had forgotten how angry he was with her.

18
00:01:40.798 --> 00:01:45.872
Wanting to please her, he went to get the medicine off the shelf.

19
00:01:45.873 --> 00:01:49.771
"Don't do that!" screamed Tinker Bell.

20
00:01:49.772 --> 00:01:56.372
She had heard Hook muttering as he went through the forest, and she had learned about the poison.

21
00:01:56.373 --> 00:01:59.722
"Why not?" asked Peter.

22
00:01:59.723 --> 00:02:05.113
"Your medicine is poisoned. Hook did it while you slept," she said.

23
00:02:05.114 --> 00:02:10.947
"Don't be silly," Peter said. "You know that no grown-up can enter here."

24
00:02:10.948 --> 00:02:17.975
Tinker Bell could not explain how Hook had done it because she didn't know the secret of Slightly's tree.

25
00:02:17.976 --> 00:02:26.384
"Besides," said Peter, not wanting to admit that he had cried and fallen asleep, "I never fell asleep."

26
00:02:26.385 --> 00:02:36.496
He raised the cup to his lips. Like a bolt of lightning, Tinker Bell flew between his lips and the liquid. She drank the whole cup.

27
00:02:36.497 --> 00:02:40.892
"How dare you drink my medicine!" he yelled.

28
00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:43.745
But Tinker Bell did not answer.

29
00:02:43.746 --> 00:02:47.593
Already she was fluttering dizzily in the air.

30
00:02:47.594 --> 00:02:53.063
"What's the matter with you?" asked Peter, suddenly afraid.

31
00:02:53.064 --> 00:03:01.257
"I told you," she said softly. "It was poisoned, and now I'm going to die."

32
00:03:01.258 --> 00:03:09.042
"Oh, Tink, you drank the poison to save my life," he said. "Why did you do it?"

33
00:03:09.043 --> 00:03:14.061
"Don't be silly, Peter," she whispered. "You know why."

34
00:03:14.062 --> 00:03:18.632
Tinker Bell flew slowly to her nook and lay on her bed.

35
00:03:18.633 --> 00:03:23.479
As Peter watched, her light grew fainter and fainter.

36
00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:28.658
For the second time in just a few hours, Peter began to cry.

37
00:03:28.659 --> 00:03:33.814
Tink's voice, now very low, stopped his tears for a moment.

38
00:03:33.815 --> 00:03:41.303
"If enough children believe in fairies," she told him, "I know I will get well again."

39
00:03:41.304 --> 00:03:46.248
There were no children left in the house, but Peter knew what he could do.

40
00:03:46.249 --> 00:03:49.943
He called out to all the children who might be dreaming.

41
00:03:49.944 --> 00:03:56.250
Peter knew that in their dreams children were nearer to Neverland than anyone imagined.

42
00:03:56.251 --> 00:04:03.472
"Do you believe?" he shouted. "If you do, please clap your hands!"

43
00:04:03.473 --> 00:04:08.604
Never before had Peter said "please" in such a sincere way.

44
00:04:08.605 --> 00:04:14.876
He stretched out his arms and cried, "Don't let Tinker Bell die!"

45
00:04:14.877 --> 00:04:19.526
Suddenly there was a roar of clapping from around the world.

46
00:04:19.527 --> 00:04:27.736
And as parents all over rushed to their children's rooms to see what was the matter, Tinker Bell sat up in bed.

47
00:04:27.737 --> 00:04:38.858
Her light was bright once again. Peter had saved her!

